INSERT INTO "Requirement" (id, "requirementId", "familyId", title, "basicRequirement", discussion, "furtherDiscussion", "exampleOne", "exampleTwo", "potentialAssessmentConsiderations", "keyReferences", "cmmcLevel", "sortOrder", "createdAt", "updatedAt")
VALUES ('w37mq3g8cwvzveqpjoljgalb', '03.11.03', 'zpw6zzbkw8tymcs6g71o1why', 'Vulnerability Remediation', $body$Remediate vulnerabilities in accordance with risk assessments.$body$, $body$Vulnerabilities discovered, for example, via the scanning conducted in response to RA.L2-
3.11.2, are remediated with consideration of the related assessment of risk. The 
consideration of risk influences the prioritization of remediation efforts and the level of 
effort to be expended in the remediation for specific vulnerabilities.$body$, $body$Not all vulnerabilities captured in a vulnerability scanner may pose the same level of risk to 
an organization. Prioritize mitigation efforts to close the most critical vulnerabilities first. 


Track all vulnerability remediation to ensure completion; also track vulnerabilities that you 
have determined not to remediate. 

This requirement, RA.L2-3.11.3, benefits from CA.L2-3.12.2. RA.L2-3.11.3 allows 
remediation of vulnerabilities to take place based on the developed plans of actions for 
vulnerabilities from CA.L2-3.12.2.$body$, $body$You are a system administrator. Each quarter you receive a list of vulnerabilities generated 
by your company’s vulnerability scanner [a]. You prioritize that list and note which 
vulnerabilities should be targeted as soon as possible as well as which vulnerabilities you 
can safely defer addressing at this time. You document the reasoning behind accepting the 
risk of the unremediated flaws and note to continue to monitor these vulnerabilities in case 
you need to revise the decision at a later date [b].$body$, NULL, $body$• Are the results of risk assessments used to prioritize vulnerabilities for remediation [b]? 
• For any given vulnerability is action taken for remediation, acceptance, avoidance, or 
transference of the vulnerability risk [b]? 
• Are all high risk vulnerabilities prioritized [b]?$body$, $body$• NIST SP 800-171 Rev. 2 3.11.3$body$, 'LEVEL_2', 3, NOW(), NOW())
